    "gitCommitHash": "4af8e4361e7464b95666a79c7bfdf6540840303c",
    "gitCommitMessage": "Full-screen Ship/Return scanner: camera fills the screen, readout + SHIP/RETURN overlay it\n\nThe scan loop had a fixed 36%-height camera box with the mode toggle, a permanently-visible last-scan card (full chips/banner on every single scan, including plain ones), the whole order list, Undo and Submit all stacked below it. Reference: the old app's Ship scan screen (screenshots), plus the explicit ask for a full-bleed camera with a scan border and two separate SHIP/RETURN boxes over the live feed rather than sections underneath it.\n\nCamera is now full-screen; header and a bottom readout+SHIP/RETURN overlay are drawn over it via Scanner's own children prop. A plain accepted scan now shows just the barcode, large — the full colour-bar/chips/banner card is reserved for cases that need judgement (duplicate, customer code, unrecognised barcode, odd asset status). The order list/Remove/Undo/Submit moved into a review sheet opened via a header pill (tap count), since they are reviewed occasionally, not read continuously. Scanner gained controlsBottomInset so its own torch/zoom/Snap/Read-text stack clears the new bottom overlay (measured via onLayout, not guessed).\n\ntsc --noEmit and npm test both pass clean.",
